  471|  5.69M|                // of the DFA state. Tracking them is actually superfluous;
  472|  5.69M|                // they won't cause any harm other than making determinization
  473|  5.69M|                // slower.
  474|  5.69M|                //
  475|  5.69M|                // Why aren't these needed? Well, in an NFA, epsilon
  476|  5.69M|                // transitions are really just jumping points to other states.
  477|  5.69M|                // So once you hit an epsilon transition, the same set of
  478|  5.69M|                // resulting states always appears. Therefore, putting them in
  479|  5.69M|                // a DFA's set of ordered NFA states is strictly redundant.
  480|  5.69M|                //
  481|  5.69M|                // Look-around states are also epsilon transitions, but
  482|  5.69M|                // they are *conditional*. So their presence could be
