  497|  5.69M|                // epsilon closure to account for look-ahead in 'next' *only
  498|  5.69M|                // when necessary*. Namely, only when the set of look-around
  499|  5.69M|                // assertions changes and only when those changes are within
  500|  5.69M|                // the set of assertions that are needed in order to step
  501|  5.69M|                // through the closure correctly. Otherwise, if we re-do the
  502|  5.69M|                // epsilon closure needlessly, it could change based on the
  503|  5.69M|                // fact that we are omitting epsilon states here.
