  505|  5.69M|                // -----
  506|  5.69M|                //
  507|  5.69M|                // Welp, scratch the above. It turns out that recording these
  508|  5.69M|                // is in fact necessary to seemingly handle one particularly
  509|  5.69M|                // annoying case: when a conditional epsilon transition is
  510|  5.69M|                // put inside of a repetition operator. One specific case I
